  "usage_note": "**Underneath** before a noun (*underneath the table*) is a preposition, a separate entry; this entry covers the word with no noun after it. In the first sense it often comes at the end of the clause (*look underneath*) or just after a noun (*the wood underneath*); in the second it usually comes near the start (*but underneath he was afraid*).",
